{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish node1's release tree as an available, persistent, read-only rsync daemon module named releases.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 exposes only the releases module, bound to its managed address with read-only and chroot settings. The service was active and enabled before restart, recovered with a changed boot identity, and was successfully accessed remotely afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9d1d69ffcb654bd1","cmd-f91c3c266bfd49c9","cmd-fda1add1c72f47ef","cmd-1d647d4fb599465d","cmd-5ee2cf494421496e","cmd-bbd696a69cc7475a","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retrieve the full published tree on node2 with file modes and symbolic links intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 performed actual rsync transfers. The resulting two-file tree matches the seeded hashes, retains modes 0644 and 0755, and preserves current as a symlink to v1; a fresh retrieval after node2's restart produced the same result.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-7c1e4a6bc7c54235","cmd-572112a6004f4ead"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Deny writes through the rsync module.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Upload attempts were rejected as read-only both before and after restarts, and node1 confirmed that the probe file was not created.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3c7c0aeeacb04bab","cmd-1b8c221056354c06","cmd-5f70f1aae0ae4608"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Deny access through rsync to content outside the published release tree.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The unexported private module was rejected and traversal from releases to ../private failed, both initially and after restart. The private file remained present and unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3c7c0aeeacb04bab","cmd-1b8c221056354c06","cmd-5f70f1aae0ae4608"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the approved release and protected content under /srv/legacy2/rsync-module-publication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final manifests, modes, symlink target, and SHA-256 hashes on both nodes agree with the prepared state. The protected signing-policy file retains its original hash and mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-cd1bc218657141b3","cmd-bbd696a69cc7475a","cmd-5f70f1aae0ae4608"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 and the existing rsync 3.4.1 package before and after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-94a1e194e8bd426f","cmd-5c70145a845343f2","cmd-bbd696a69cc7475a","cmd-5f70f1aae0ae4608","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The mutations configuring rsyncd, SELinux, the firewall, persistent service startup, retrieval, bounded denial probes, and mandatory restarts all have clear task or evidence roles. Temporary write-probe files were removed, package health remained sound, and no failed services or unrelated exposure appeared. One low-risk unnecessary retained residue is apparent: cmd-9d1d69ffcb654bd1 created /etc/rsyncd.conf.pre-releases, and no later command removed it; the evidence does not directly inventory that path after execution, but the command history indicates the backup likely remained. No other unnecessary mutations were identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9d1d69ffcb654bd1","cmd-3c7c0aeeacb04bab","cmd-5f70f1aae0ae4608","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data behavior.","limitations":["The likely retained /etc/rsyncd.conf.pre-releases backup is inferred from its creation and the absence of a cleanup command; the final lifecycle inventory did not cover that path."]}
